# Rydar doc evolution

This repo's documentation is the context layer the whole project is built from. It evolves with every change. A change that leaves a spec describing something that is no longer true is incomplete.

## Before you start

Read [README.md](../../README.md) for the doc map, then [PRODUCT.md](../../PRODUCT.md) and [docs/DOMAIN.md](../../docs/DOMAIN.md). Every other spec uses the domain model's vocabulary, so reading them first is what keeps a change from using the wrong words.

Full working guide is [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

## Hard rules

- Never invent a value marked `TBD`. Colors, fonts, spacing, zoom tiers, durations, deep link schemes, staleness windows. A task needing one is blocked on a decision. Say so.
- Never fabricate a fare. No averaging across providers, no interpolation, no placeholder prices. A provider without a price shows a typed reason.
- `core/` imports nothing from `platform/` or `app/`.
- Never put a provider name in a conditional in feature code. It belongs in the registry in `core/providers`.

## Before finishing any change

1. Walk the doc impact table in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and update every doc your change contradicts.
2. On each touched doc, bump `version`, set `updated`, and add a `## Changelog` line saying what changed. All three must agree.
3. A new document must be added to the doc map in `README.md` in the same change.
4. A choice that closed off an alternative needs an ADR in `docs/DECISIONS/`, from the template, listed in the ADR index.
5. Run `node tools/check-docs.mjs`.

## In your summary

State which docs you updated and which you considered and deliberately left alone. A change that claims no doc impact should say why, because that is usually where a missed update hides.
